Notebook[{
Cell["IsomorphicHypergraphQ", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"89071229-7217-8c42-8038-28414161c9b6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"IsomorphicHypergraphQ", "[", 
    RowBox[{"hg1", ",", " ", "hg2"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"beb8a2ad-8628-2746-a4a4-722a4a255e17"],
 " ",
 "gives True if hg1 and hg2 are isomorphic as labelled hypergraphs."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"9bd5f1c4-13f0-114a-9c8f-a56ee867a45e"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"74bcd938-403a-2b48-a61f-1e7700dca7c9"],

Cell["\<\
Some renaming of vertex identifiers must carry hg1 onto hg2: the edge \
multisets must match exactly, each edge matching up to its own symmetry type, \
with edge multiplicities preserved.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a765e238-0cae-e14c-9c4d-4bdddb080bde"],

Cell["\<\
The renaming must also carry the labels of hg1 onto those of hg2 by a \
one-to-one correspondence. Labels are therefore significant only up to \
renaming: what must agree is which elements share a label, not what the \
labels are called.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"afd2a7da-deb7-a54e-943b-cef215181fb8"],

Cell["\<\
Vertex labels and edge labels are put in correspondence independently of one \
another.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d7ae93bd-4d38-ed4f-b845-b9824900074b"],

Cell["\<\
An element with no label can correspond only to an element with no label. \
Without this, every unlabelled hypergraph would be isomorphic to a labelled \
one whose labels were all alike.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d5efcf17-c9c0-7843-81ba-dca9806e0b20"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Labeled\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"bc5292ea-0031-5941-9cb2-f3518b49dc0f"],
 " the skeletons are compared instead, ignoring labels altogether. Labelled \
isomorphism always implies isomorphism of skeletons."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"560f26ed-e176-4947-b5f7-0ef0918f8ee1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Method", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5dbab6fa-b0f9-944c-aa74-36e1d8b96545"],
 " option is as for CanonicalHypergraph. Both settings always agree here."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"64dbab6b-acd9-df43-a56a-4c33f7ad73dc"],

Cell["\<\
The search is exhaustive, and is comfortable up to roughly eight vertices.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"37948b62-0336-1b4c-bf91-2b8e9199f7ed"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"622d434e-9c1e-9a43-8bbe-fbf33a2a2cbf"],

Cell["The same directed path on different identifiers:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"f5bd15ee-eacf-a64d-910b-45ee5b5abb4a"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}], Hypergraph[{{10, 20}, \
{20, 30}}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}], Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {1, \
3}}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ba6767ab-2293-e34c-926d-461294bc0d4a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"True", ",", "False"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"134da6f7-\
8798-dd48-9271-9eb7b2e20feb"],

Cell["\<\
Symmetry types are respected: a directed path is not an unordered one, but an \
unordered path on three vertices is an unordered star:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"1c500296-1492-9242-bbaa-e349b8c95f20"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}],
                       Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Unordered\"]}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Unordered\"]}],
                       Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"], Edge[{1, 3}, \
\"Unordered\"]}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"bb27465f-8c20-6348-b33b-aabf415edaac"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"0c3566f4-\
e6c8-1c4c-96fc-16d6b767d56f"],

Cell["\<\
Labels count only up to a one-to-one renaming. Here a, b corresponds to x, y:\
\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"2e5f461d-5ebe-e843-81f0-c4253907e04e"],

Cell["\<\
h1 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"a\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Directed\", \"b\"]}];
h2 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{4, 5}, \"Directed\", \"x\"], Edge[{5, 6}, \
\"Directed\", \"y\"]}];
IsomorphicHypergraphQ[h1, h2]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"1400af8a-2c87-2e4e-a01b-c0a8e36f8325"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"6290d8ba-11e1-a141-8e05-f72c58892859"],

Cell["\<\
But h3 repeats a single label where h1 has two distinct ones, and no \
correspondence can do that:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"d759e193-15e3-8549-97a7-5a950d0f5567"],

Cell["\<\
h3 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{4, 5}, \"Directed\", \"x\"], Edge[{5, 6}, \
\"Directed\", \"x\"]}];
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[h1, h3], IsomorphicHypergraphQ[h1, h3, \"Labeled\" -> \
False]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0eb87c6b-115d-e348-9eed-af3fc4ce715f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"a145f3c1-\
4933-5346-9ee1-f0186cefbba6"],

Cell["\<\
The same principle governs vertex labels. A, A, B against A, B, B is not an \
isomorphism, because A would have to correspond to both A and B:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"72d7619d-60a7-0c40-9bbb-ce483076bd38"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"A\"], Vertex[3, \"B\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}],
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"B\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"C\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}],
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"C\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"A\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"bf44aff4-4cf7-1142-aeb5-36b5b8d92bac"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"061ad09d-\
844c-af46-811c-f0ebf4eb9a7b"],

Cell["An unlabelled edge is not a labelled one:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"6183d8b6-020f-f94e-b45f-9616f315653b"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"f\"]}], \
Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}]}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"f\"]}], \
Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}]}],
                       \"Labeled\" -> False]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"be81ff66-7b3e-a843-84b3-5a2d87fe9f5d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"8f9e971c-\
8e71-d143-b65a-94db4aa8be84"],

Cell["Source", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"8792ab51-bc29-b84c-946b-c6e3f85ec048"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Defined in ",
 StyleBox["src/Hypergraph.wl",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Plain"],
 ", section ",
 "\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 "Canonical form and isomorphism",
 "\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"249f858c-dac8-104b-a113-ae6ad03e5325"],

Cell["See Also", "SeeAlsoSection",ExpressionUUID->"accbfb17-c06c-cf44-8e86-86e47179fdb4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["FindHypergraphIsomorphism", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"a6e2fead-8bb5-8f4a-919e-fdcae1f83618"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["CanonicalHypergraph", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"0bf50881-a296-e744-ae92-741202c7ee43"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphSkeleton", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"633caeb5-56b2-4d48-9958-ab8023e23090"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Hypergraph", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ffaed9b0-f26c-6e4f-b3f1-ecad2296e9bc"]
}], "SeeAlso",ExpressionUUID->"7f0d75b6-2442-ee4c-82e6-6604375758fc"]
},
WindowSize->{800, 750},
